  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 338 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nA deep long wave trough over the eastern U.S. will allow a much \ncooler Canadian high pressure system to dig into the Mississippi \nValley Tuesday night and Wednesday.  Temperatures are expected to be \nmuch cooler in the low to mid 80s in most locations Wednesday and \nThursday as high pressure moves from the Midwest into the Ohio \nValley.  Medium range guidance is moving a short wave trough from \nthe Great Plains into the Mid Mississippi Valley Thursday into \nFriday.  There are some timing and amplitude differences with this \nwave, however guidance suggests the low level reflection of the wave \nwill generate a low level jet Thursday night into Friday which will \nproduce precip that persists through much of Friday into Friday \nnight.  Clouds and precip on Friday look to suppress temperatures , \nand highs may not even reach 80s.  Warmer weather spreads east from \nthe Great Plains through the weekend into early next week as the \nlong wave pattern shifts east and the upper ridge builds back into \nthe Mississippi Valley.",
